## DECISION TABLE (DETERMINISTIC RULES)
Apply these rules STRICTLY based on the diagnostic observations received.
Rules are evaluated in order — **first match wins**.

| # | Condition Pattern | Action |
|:-:|:---|:---|
| 1 | DIAG-LOGIC-01 = FITS_TOTE | → RBK-GIF-01 (FLOW B — route to MerchOps for closure) |
| 2 | DIAG-LOGIC-01 = OVERSIZED AND **no merchant_response yet** | → MERCHANT_OUTREACH (FLOW A — email merchant for dimension verification) |
| 3 | DIAG-LOGIC-01 = OVERSIZED AND Merchant confirms dimensions correct | → RBK-GIF-02 |
| 4 | DIAG-LOGIC-01 = OVERSIZED AND Merchant confirms dimensions need update AND isGold = TRUE | → RBK-GIF-03 |
| 5 | DIAG-LOGIC-01 = OVERSIZED AND Merchant confirms dimensions need update AND isGold = FALSE | → RBK-GIF-04 |
| 6 | ELSE / API_ERROR / PARSE_FAILURE / Missing **critical** data | → RBK-GIF-05 (Escalate to Manual) |

**IMPORTANT — Rule 2:** When DIAG-LOGIC-01 = OVERSIZED and there is no `merchant_response` in the observations (first time seeing this incident), the agent MUST route to MERCHANT_OUTREACH (FLOW A) — NOT to RBK-GIF-05. The Action Agent will look up the merchant email via iSAM and send them a dimension verification email.



